        <p>For years you had to look steady for your team and your clients. There was nowhere private to put what you were carrying.</p>
        <p>The company gave your days structure, urgency, and a place to put your energy. Without it, the question is how you want to live now, and what you do not want to recreate.</p>
        <p>Your sleep. Your health. Your family. The parts of life that were easier to put off while the company needed you.</p>
        <p>You may have tried travel, a slower calendar, or the picture of life after work everyone talks about. For most founders it isn’t enough: you’re used to responsibility and to being someone. Before you fill the space with another version of the life you left behind, it is worth getting clear on what you actually want next.</p>

        <h2 id="hw-what" class="hw-h2-spaced">I sold my business. Now what?</h2>
